src/single-sided-lp/AbstractSingleSidedLP.sol:getWithdrawRequestValue|class=C15|High|An external attacker flash-swaps the 2-token Curve pool so one leg's proportional payout truncates to zero, calls initiateWithdraw (which silently skips that leg via if (exitBalances[i] == 0) continue;), leaving a one-legged request that makes hasPendingWithdrawals true while getWithdrawRequestValue's require(hasRequest) over ALL of TOKENS() reverts — so convertToAssets permanently reverts and the maxed-out leveraged position can never be priced, redeemed, or liquidated, stranding the debt as a loss to the money market.|src/single-sided-lp/AbstractSingleSidedLP.sol|<work>/notional/zone-hunt-out/verify/gates/16_src_single_sided_lp_AbstractSingleSidedLP_sol_getWithdrawRequestValue/aux.sol
